{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNPgk9cEwPv4YihBx9bA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #323 as `done`: the engineer triage role writes the plan and the `engineer` worker implements it. The decision is in `.ard/323/triage-lead.md`.\n\n- **Ready to start:** the issue depends on part A (#322), and that has already landed on main (commit `c5d12ce`, PR #354), so nothing blocks it.\n- **Why only the engineer:** it is the only triage role besides lead that exists. The change spans several packages (gitx, committer, worker, servecmd, the starter config and the proposal doc), but there is no architect role to send it to. The engineer has the earlier plan for #255 to work from.\n\nThings for a maintainer, also listed under Open issues in the file:\n- **Security:** the change alters the committer's guards for two-parent merge commits: the path check, the staged-change check and the lease push. The PR needs a close human review on top of eng-review, which runs on every PR anyway.\n- **Merge order:** the conflict-round section of the worker prompt is left out of this issue on purpose. It has to land as a separate human PR, with or before this one. Otherwise the switch gets turned on before the worker has any prompt guidance for conflict rounds."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":797,"cache_read_input_tokens":12763,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":797},"output_tokens":389,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f25e777-fd3f-411e-a5b7-29980cf70e6d","uuid":"12d28ba1-3fca-42b4-b689-129b0d1a40fb","timestamp":"2026-11-24T20:34:22.471Z","request_id":"req_011ChNPgjpX1jL7vWGFWGzpm"}
